## Architecture Changes

The new module integrates cleanly into the existing architecture without replacing any existing abstractions:

```
POST /api/v1/research/query
         │
         ▼
  QueryUnderstandingService          app/query_understanding/service.py
         │  depends on (protocol only)
         ▼
  LLMProvider                        app/domain/interfaces.py
         │
         ▼
  OpenAILLMProvider                  app/providers/llm/openai_provider.py
         │  returns raw dict
         ▼
  QueryUnderstandingLLMOutput        app/query_understanding/schemas.py
  (Pydantic validation)
         │  maps to domain
         ▼
  QueryUnderstanding                 app/domain/models/query_understanding.py
         │  attached to
         ▼
  ResearchQuery.understanding        app/domain/models/query.py
         │  + expanded_queries[]
         ▼
  ResearchPipeline (Stage 1)         app/orchestration/research_pipeline.py
```

**Key design decisions:**
- `QueryUnderstandingLLMOutput` (LLM schema) and `QueryUnderstanding` (domain model) are **intentionally separate** — the LLM contract can evolve without touching the domain.
- The service depends on the `LLMProvider` **protocol** only — swapping to Gemini/Anthropic requires zero changes to business logic.
- `ResearchQuery` is returned as an immutable copy (`model_copy`) — the original is never mutated.
- The pipeline fails **gracefully** on `ProviderError` — returning a `FAILED` result rather than raising.

